1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,950
If AI ever answered you with perfect confidence

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,950
and you almost pasted it into a slide, email, or assignment —

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,950
this lesson is your seatbelt.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,950
Don't trust fluency.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,950
Today: one idea, one skill, one action.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,950
Confidence without gullibility.

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,950
Picture this.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,950
You're finishing a presentation for class or a Monday update

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,950
for your manager.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,950
AI gives you a clean line:

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,950
"Studies show 73% of teams improved productivity in two weeks.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,950
"

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,950
It sounds research-ish.

14
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,950
It sounds sendable.

15
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,950
You almost drop it into the deck.

16
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,950
Then something nags —

17
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,950
and you search.

18
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,950
No study. Wrong number. Or a name that doesn't exist.

19
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,950
I've seen students and professionals catch this one minute

20
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,950
before send —

21
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,950
and I've seen the version where they didn't.

22
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,950
Here's the truth:

23
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,950
embarrassment rarely comes from using AI.

24
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,950
It comes from outsourcing verification.

25
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:16,950
The problem isn't that AI makes mistakes.

26
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:26,950
The problem is that mistakes arrive wearing fluent clothing.

27
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:36,950
Your brain treats smooth language as credible language.

28
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:46,950
That's normal.

29
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:56,950
It's also dangerous.

30
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:06,950
So separate three checks before anything leaves your hands:

31
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:16,950
Source — Where did this claim live outside the chat?

32
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:26,950
Number — Can I confirm the figure in a reliable place?

33
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:36,950
Name — Are people, companies, laws, and book titles real and

34
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:46,950
correctly spelled?

35
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:56,950
If any check fails, cut or correct.

36
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:06,950
Fluency is not proof.

37
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,664
Here's the skill.

38
00:04:12,714 --> 00:04:18,379
Framework name: VERIFY

39
00:04:18,429 --> 00:04:24,093
Step 1 — Source.

40
00:04:24,143 --> 00:04:29,807
Highlight every claim that isn't from your own files.

41
00:04:29,857 --> 00:04:35,521
Ask: can I open a source that isn't this chat?

42
00:04:35,571 --> 00:04:41,236
If the model won't show a real link you can open — treat it as

43
00:04:41,286 --> 00:04:46,950
unverified.

44
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:52,664
Step 2 — Number.

45
00:04:52,714 --> 00:04:58,379
Circle every percentage, date, price, and statistic.

46
00:04:58,429 --> 00:05:04,093
Confirm against a primary page, your spreadsheet, or a trusted report.

47
00:05:04,143 --> 00:05:09,807
No confirmation — no number.

48
00:05:09,857 --> 00:05:15,521
Step 3 — Name.

49
00:05:15,571 --> 00:05:21,236
Check people, organisations, laws, place names, and titles.

50
00:05:21,286 --> 00:05:26,950
One wrong name can sink a good email.

51
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:32,664
Demo: take an AI paragraph, strike the fancy statistic,

52
00:05:32,714 --> 00:05:38,379
replace with a fact from your own notes, keep the useful

53
00:05:38,429 --> 00:05:44,093
structure.

54
00:05:44,143 --> 00:05:49,807
That is VERIFY.

55
00:05:49,857 --> 00:05:55,521
Source. Number. Name.

56
00:05:55,571 --> 00:06:01,236
You stop fearing AI —

57
00:06:01,286 --> 00:06:06,950
and you stop being fooled by it.

58
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:15,521
Quick psychology — not as a diagnosis, as a tool.

59
00:06:15,571 --> 00:06:24,093
Confidence can be borrowed.

60
00:06:24,143 --> 00:06:32,664
When text sounds assured, we borrow that assurance into our body.

61
00:06:32,714 --> 00:06:41,236
Verification returns ownership to you.

62
00:06:41,286 --> 00:06:49,807
You become the adult in the room again.

63
00:06:49,857 --> 00:06:58,379
Borrowed confidence is risky.

64
00:06:58,429 --> 00:07:06,950
Earned confidence is checked.

65
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:13,617
Your action today — under thirty minutes:

66
00:07:13,667 --> 00:07:20,283
1. Take one AI answer you planned to use.

67
00:07:20,333 --> 00:07:26,950
2. Run Source · Number · Name.

68
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:33,617
3. Correct or cut anything unverified, then save the clean version.

69
00:07:33,667 --> 00:07:40,283
When you're done, you will not be cynical.

70
00:07:40,333 --> 00:07:46,950
You will be FutureHer-ready: calm, sharp, and hard to embarrass.

71
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:53,617
Subscribe to Forward Notes for calm weekly readiness,

72
00:07:53,667 --> 00:08:00,283
and join The Forward Collective if you want a place to

73
00:08:00,333 --> 00:08:06,950
practise verification together.

74
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:12,950
Next time we shift into Money —

75
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:18,950
what to do when your salary disappears before month-end.

76
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:24,950
Dignity first. A map second.
